{# ============================================================================
   ACM CERTIFICATE DIGEST EMAIL TEMPLATE - EDITING GUIDE
   ============================================================================
   This Jinja2 template generates the HTML email for the ACM Certs Digest.
   Because email clients (Outlook, Gmail, etc.) strip standard <style> blocks,
   ALL CSS must be written inline using style="..." attributes.

   HOW TO MAKE COMMON EDITS:

   1. ADDING A NEW COLUMN (e.g., 'Region' or 'Account ID'):
      - Go to the `cert_table` macro below.
      - Add a new <th> tag in the header row (e.g., <th>Region</th>).
      - Add a corresponding <td> tag in the loop (e.g., <td>{{ row.region }}</td>).

   2. CHANGING THE CRITICAL EXPIRY HIGHLIGHT (Currently 7 days):
      - In the `cert_table` macro, look for the `row_bg` variable definition
        and the text color logic: `days <= 7`.
      - Change the `7` to your new threshold (e.g., `days <= 10`).

   3. CHANGING COLORS:
      - Look for the hex codes in the inline styles or the `row_bg` variable.
      - Red/Failed: #fdecea (bg), #b71c1c (text/border)
      - Amber/Expiring: #fff8e1 (bg), #8a6d00 (text), #f0e0a0 (border)
      - Green/Renewed: #eaf6ea (bg), #1b5e20 (text), #bfdcbf (border)
   ============================================================================ #}

{# templates/acm_digest_mail.html.j2
   Consolidated ACM certificate digest.
   Expects: failed_rows, expiring_rows, renewed_rows, missing_reports,
            digest_expiry_days, expected_reports, digest_certs
   Inline styles only — email clients strip <style> blocks. #}
{# EXPIRY COLOUR BANDS (v2) — applied to the Expiring table only (accent
   'amber'). Failures stay red and Renewed stays green regardless of how
   few days are left, because days_left is the expiry of the cert as it was
   found in ACM BEFORE the import: a successfully renewed cert still carries
   the old date and would otherwise render red in the Renewed table.
     <= 7 days  -> #ff9999 (deep red)
     <= 10 days -> #fdecea (red)
     11-15 days -> #fff8e1 (yellow)                                          #}
{% set band_critical = 7 %}
{% set band_red = 10 %}
{# Console-link settings are resolved HERE, at template top level, and passed
   INTO the macro as arguments. Do not move these inside the macro: a macro
   body does not reliably see playbook variables, so aws_console_role read
   from in there comes back empty and every link silently falls back to the
   plain console URL. Top level always sees them. #}
{% set console_portal = aws_console_portal | default('aws-saasmstr', true) %}
{% set console_role = aws_console_role | default('', true) %}
{% macro cert_table(rows, accent, console_portal='aws-saasmstr', console_role='') -%}
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;margin-bottom:24px;">
  <tr style="background:#f0f0f0;">
    <th style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;">Client / Env</th>
    <th style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;">Domain</th>
    <th style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;">Expiry (UTC)</th>
    <th style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:right;">Days left</th>
    <th style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:center;">In use</th>
    <th style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:center;">Renewal</th>
    <th style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;">Status</th>
  </tr>
{% for row in rows %}
{% set days = (row.days_left | int) if (row.days_left | string | length) > 0 else none %}
{% set row_bg = '#fdecea' if accent == 'red'
   else ('#eaf6ea' if accent == 'green'
   else ('#ff9999' if (days is not none and days <= band_critical)
   else ('#fdecea' if (days is not none and days <= band_red)
   else ('#fff8e1' if accent == 'amber' else '#ffffff')))) %}
{# Region, ACCOUNT and certificate id all come out of the ARN we already
   publish — arn:aws:acm:<region>:<account>:certificate/<cert_id> — so no
   extra artifact field is needed. The domain cell is left as plain text on
   purpose (mail clients auto-linkify hostnames and would fight an anchor of
   ours); the console link hangs off the line beneath instead.

   WHY THE ACCOUNT ID IS SHOWN: a plain console URL carries NO account
   context. It opens in whichever account the reader's browser session is
   already signed into, so with many accounts every link lands in the same
   one and reports "certificate not found".

   LINK FORM: when aws_console_role is set, the link goes through the IAM
   Identity Center access portal, which switches to the account named in the
   ARN and then lands on the certificate. Without it the link is the plain
   console URL (wrong account, but the account id beside it tells the reader
   which one to switch to). Set in aws-client-vars-base.yml:

     aws_console_role: <permission set name, e.g. AdministratorAccess>
     aws_console_portal: aws-saasmstr        # default, override if it moves

   aws_console_role is a PERMISSION SET name, not the full IAM role. Readers
   who do not hold that permission set in that account land on the portal
   rather than the certificate — a soft failure, not a broken link.

   console_portal / console_role arrive as MACRO ARGUMENTS — see the note
   above the macro definition for why they are not read here. #}
{% set arn = row.cert_arn | default('', true) | string %}
{% set arn_parts = arn.split(':') %}
{% set cert_region = arn_parts[3] if (arn_parts | length) > 5 else '' %}
{% set cert_account = arn_parts[4] if (arn_parts | length) > 5 else '' %}
{% set cert_id = arn.split('/')[-1] if '/' in arn else '' %}
  <tr style="background:{{ row_bg }};">
{# client_env_label is set by the digest's ARN dedupe and lists every client
   environment sharing one certificate ('hxtx / np, prd'). Falls back to the
   single pair so rows from an older artifact still render. #}
    <td style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;white-space:nowrap;">{{ row.client_env_label | default(row.client ~ ' / ' ~ row.env, true) }}</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;">{{ row.domain }}
{%- if cert_region | length > 0 and cert_id | length > 0 %}
{%- set console_url = 'https://' ~ cert_region ~ '.console.aws.amazon.com/acm/certificates/' ~ cert_id -%}
{%- if console_role | length > 0 and cert_account | length > 0 -%}
{%- set cert_link = 'https://' ~ console_portal ~ '.awsapps.com/start/#/console?account_id=' ~ cert_account ~ '&amp;role_name=' ~ console_role ~ '&amp;destination=' ~ (console_url | urlencode) -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set cert_link = console_url -%}
{%- endif -%}
<br/><a href="{{ cert_link }}" style="font-size:11px;color:#5b5bd6;text-decoration:none;">{{ cert_region }} &middot; {{ cert_account }} &middot; {{ cert_id[:8] }} &#8599;</a>{% endif %}</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;">{{ row.not_after | default('-', true) }}</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:right;{% if days is not none and days <= band_critical %}color:#b71c1c;font-weight:bold;{% endif %}">{{ days if days is not none else '-' }}</td>
{# in_use: 'yes' / 'no' / '-' . Older artifacts (jobs still on the previous
   code) have no in_use key, so default to '-' rather than erroring. #}
{% set used = row.in_use | default('-', true) | string | lower %}
    <td style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:center;{% if used == 'no' %}color:#6b6b6b;{% endif %}">{{ 'Yes' if used in ['yes','true'] else ('No' if used in ['no','false'] else '-') }}</td>
{# renewal: 'automated' = configured in tools.yml / the group's records, this
   workflow renews it. 'manual' = found by the account-wide sweep, ineligible
   for AWS auto-renewal, nobody renews it — someone has to act. Older
   artifacts have no renewal key, so default to '-'. #}
{% set renewal = row.renewal | default('', true) | string | lower %}
    <td style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:center;{% if renewal == 'manual' %}color:#b71c1c;font-weight:bold;{% endif %}">{{ 'Automated' if renewal == 'automated' else ('Manual' if renewal == 'manual' else '-') }}</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;">{{ row.status }}{% if row.error | default('', true) | length > 0 %}<br/><span style="color:#b71c1c;font-size:12px;">{{ row.error }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
  </tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{%- endmacro %}
<div style="font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;max-width:900px;">
  <h2 style="margin:0 0 4px 0;">ACM Certificate Digest &mdash; {{ '%Y-%m-%d' | strftime }}</h2>
  <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0;color:#555;font-size:13px;">
    Consolidated daily report across {{ expected_reports | length }} client environment(s)
    &middot; {{ digest_certs | length }} distinct certificate(s) scanned
    &middot; expiry window: {{ digest_expiry_days }} days
{%- if (digest_duplicates_collapsed | default(0) | int) > 0 %}
    &middot; {{ digest_duplicates_collapsed }} duplicate row(s) collapsed
{%- endif %}
  </p>

  <p style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 20px 0;">
    <span style="background:#fdecea;border:1px solid #f5c6c2;border-radius:4px;padding:3px 10px;margin-right:6px;">&#10060; Failed: <b>{{ failed_rows | length }}</b></span>
    <span style="background:#fff8e1;border:1px solid #f0e0a0;border-radius:4px;padding:3px 10px;margin-right:6px;">&#9200; Expiring &le; {{ digest_expiry_days }}d: <b>{{ expiring_rows | length }}</b></span>
    <span style="background:#eaf6ea;border:1px solid #bfdcbf;border-radius:4px;padding:3px 10px;margin-right:6px;">&#9989; Renewed: <b>{{ renewed_rows | length }}</b></span>
    <span style="background:#ededed;border:1px solid #cccccc;border-radius:4px;padding:3px 10px;">&#10067; No report: <b>{{ missing_reports | length }}</b></span>
  </p>

{% if failed_rows | length > 0 %}
  <h3 style="color:#b71c1c;margin:0 0 8px 0;">&#10060; Failures &mdash; manual action required</h3>
  <p style="font-size:12px;color:#555;margin:0 0 8px 0;">Import failures and chain-verification failures also triggered immediate individual alerts.</p>
  {{ cert_table(failed_rows, 'red', console_portal, console_role) }}
{% endif %}

{% if expiring_rows | length > 0 %}
  <h3 style="color:#8a6d00;margin:0 0 8px 0;">&#9200; Expiring within {{ digest_expiry_days }} days (not yet renewed)</h3>
  {{ cert_table(expiring_rows | sort(attribute='days_left'), 'amber', console_portal, console_role) }}
{% endif %}

{% if renewed_rows | length > 0 %}
  <h3 style="color:#1b5e20;margin:0 0 8px 0;">&#9989; Renewed in this run</h3>
  {{ cert_table(renewed_rows, 'green', console_portal, console_role) }}
{% endif %}

{% if missing_reports | length > 0 %}
  <h3 style="color:#b71c1c;margin:0 0 8px 0;">&#10067; Client environments with NO report</h3>
  <p style="font-size:12px;color:#555;margin:0 0 8px 0;">
    These branches finished without publishing a report (job failed or errored
    before collection). Their certificates were NOT checked today &mdash; treat
    as unknown, not healthy. Check the workflow job in AWX.
  </p>
  <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;margin-bottom:24px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f0f0;">
      <th style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;">Client</th>
      <th style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;">Env</th>
    </tr>
{% for miss in missing_reports %}
    <tr style="background:#fdecea;">
      <td style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;">{{ miss.client }}</td>
      <td style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:6px 10px;">{{ miss.env }}</td>
    </tr>
{% endfor %}
  </table>
{% endif %}

  <p style="color:#888;font-size:11px;margin-top:24px;">
    Generated by the consolidated AWS cert-renewal workflow (ACM Certs Digest Report node).
    Healthy certificates outside the {{ digest_expiry_days }}-day window are not listed;
    on fully healthy days no email is sent.
  </p>
</div>
